An agentic AI that analyzes customer behavior, value, needs, and propensity — using internal data such as savings balance, funding/lending history, and transaction patterns — to recommend a personalized interest rate for each customer purchasing TAKA Online or Deposito Online, particularly within the Emerging Affluent, Gen Z, and Millennial segments. The recommended rate/promo stays within a range pre-approved by treasury or the product owner — not fully open pricing, but controlled dynamic pricing that remains aligned with the bank's funding targets. The system also automatically filters which customers are eligible to receive dynamic rate offers, based on parameters such as balance size, cash flow stability, and tenor fit with the customer's profile. Importantly, the model includes guardrails to ensure pricing stays within risk/treasury-approved boundaries and does not result in unfair or discriminatory pricing across similar customer segments. After implementation, instead of showing the same rate to everyone, OCBC can move from "one rate for everyone" to "the right rate for the right customer at the right time" — creating greater relevance and engagement for digitally-savvy customers while keeping pricing and margin within the bank's strategic boundaries, rather than raising rates uniformly across the entire customer base, which would increase the overall cost of funds.


This dynamic pricing approach is not new — other industries such as tiket.com and Traveloka already display different prices for the same product based on demand, timing, and user segment. Funding products such as TAKA Online and Deposito Online are a natural starting point for banks to adopt this approach, as they tend to be easier to manage — their tenors are longer and liquidity is more predictable — allowing rates to be more optimal from a treasury and liquidity-management perspective, while remaining attractive to specific customers, without sacrificing product simplicity.